# Blueprint-conformance house rules — paste this block into your repo's .cursorrules.
# This repo carries an authored blueprint (see .blueprints/). Treat the gate as the done-check.

Blueprint conformance:
- This repository is gated by an authored EngineeringBlueprint in .blueprints/. The blueprint is the
  durable architectural contract; the gate is how a change proves it still holds.
- Run the gate before claiming a change is done: run `bce gate` (or the run_gate MCP tool if the
  bce-mcp server is connected). A green typecheck or test run is necessary but not sufficient — the
  change is not finished until the gate is green.
- When the gate goes red, fix the code — never silently edit the blueprint. The red names the
  violated constraint and the offending file; change the code to conform. Editing the blueprint to
  clear a red changes the contract instead of meeting it, and is a deliberate, separately-reviewed
  change, never a quiet workaround.
- Baseline changes require review. .blueprints/baseline.json records pre-existing accepted violations
  and only ever shrinks; never add a violation to it on your own initiative.
- The gate is fail-closed: there are no skip flags. If it cannot honestly grade (malformed blueprint,
  partial scan), it errors — treat an error as a red, not a pass.
